# Keeps the hub image's build context (the repo root, see
# `apps/hub/Dockerfile`'s header comment) from including build artifacts,
# node_modules and secrets — mirrors `.gitignore`.
#
# `**/` PREFIXES ARE LOAD-BEARING, NOT DECORATIVE: Docker's ignore-file
# matching (unlike `.gitignore`'s) only matches a bare pattern like
# `node_modules/` at the CONTEXT ROOT, not at every depth — VERIFIED: without
# `**/`, `packages/httpeers-qr/node_modules` (a real, already-populated
# directory in this checkout — this repo lives nested inside a multirepo
# assembly, worktrees/<name>/workspaces/httpeers, so its checked-out
# node_modules holds symlinks computed relative to the ASSEMBLY's root, two
# levels further up than this repo's own) got copied into the build context
# anyway, `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` left its stale, now-wrongly-deep
# symlinks untouched, and `tsc` failed on packages/httpeers-qr with "Cannot
# find module 'html5-qrcode'" — a broken symlink pointing above the
# filesystem root once relocated into the image. `**/node_modules/` (etc.)
# excludes every depth and forces every `node_modules` inside the image to
# come from THIS build's own `pnpm install`, at the right depth.
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/dist-ui/
**/.turbo/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git/
.env
*.key
data/
deploy/llm-appliance/data/
